quote.ab:
	      Every day he blissfully composed eight verses to Śiva Sōmanātha, the moon-bearer and Pārvati’s husband:

              his meters were all made up of five syllables;

              his lexicon came from the names of the five-faced god;

              his grammar was the purity of speech in the Śiva mantra;

              devotion to Śiva served as the ornaments of his verses.

              Composing every day, creating verses for Śiva, he lived a most wondrous life of praise of Śaṅkara, the peace-making god.
